# LF in the working tree on every OS, matching .prettierrc (endOfLine: lf) and the committed blobs. Without this, a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF and `pnpm format:check` reports thousands of false positives. Binary files are auto-detected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings, or bash fails on a Windows checkout with autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# SQL migrations must keep LF: the runner records a checksum of each file, and a CRLF checkout of the same SQL must not look "changed".
*.sql text eol=lf
